# Everything text is checked out with LF on every OS (2.11.11). The Windows release
# runner used to check out CRLF, and inline <script> hashes taken from those bytes never
# match what Chromium hashes (the HTML parser turns CRLF into LF), so every inline script
# in the Electron app was blocked by its own CSP.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wasm binary
*.onnx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.p12 binary
*.pfx binary
*.mobileprovision binary
*.car binary
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text
*.glb binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.blend binary
*.hdr binary
*.exr binary
*.env binary
